# The named theorems the library aims to capture, grouped by area. In geometry: Hopf-Rinow (a complete connected
# Riemannian manifold has geodesics between any two points). In model theory and logic: the compactness theorem (a set
# of first-order sentences has a model if every finite subset does), the Lowenheim-Skolem theorem (a theory with an
# infinite model has models of every infinite size), Herbrand's theorem (a first-order proof reduces to propositional
# logic over ground terms), and the Stone representation theorem (every Boolean algebra is the algebra of clopen sets of
# a space). Each is a claim with a proof; the machine-checked proofs in this library are the arithmetic and algebraic
# ones (the number, polynomial, order, and algebra-tower files), and these deeper theorems are recorded here as the
# targets the foundation is built toward.
